istanceToHorizon.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Geometrical distance to the horizon, Pythagorean theorem","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGeometricDistanceToHorizon.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/HomogSphElevObsZmax.png/500px-HomogSphElevObsZmax.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b7/HomogSphElevObsZmax.png/500px-HomogSphElevObsZmax.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Maximum zenith angle for elevated observer in homogeneous spherical atmosphere","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHomogSphElevObsZmax.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/HorizonDistance.png/500px-HorizonDistance.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/HorizonDistance.png/500px-HorizonDistance.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Geometrical horizon distance","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHorizonDistance.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Curvatura_2.gif/500px-Curvatura_2.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Curvatura_2.gif/1280px-Curvatura_2.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Curvatura_2.gif/500px-Curvatura_2.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A ship moving away, beyond the horizon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACurvatura_2.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/TwoPointPerspective.png/500px-TwoPointPerspectiv